<title>USA: St Joseph hogs off $1.50-2.00 - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Joseph hogs off $1.50-2.00 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>ST JOSEPH 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said compared with Tuesday, barrows and gilts were $1.50 to $2.00 lower. Top $55.50 per cwt.</p>
<p>A little warmer weather and more hogs coming to town, weakened hog prices.</p>
<p>    US 1-3     230-270 lbs    55.00-55.50, many at 55.00</p>
<p>    US 2-4  some   288 lbs    54.25</p>
<p>    US 3-4 package 298 lbs    52.00</p>
<p>Sows - not enough recently on offer for a comparison.</p>
<p>    US 1-2    300-500 lbs    45.00</p>
<p>    US 1-3    500-550 lbs    53.00</p>
<p>		  550-700 lbs    55.00-56.00</p>
<p>    Boars - 300-700 lbs    41.50</p>
<p>		200-300 lbs    42.50</p>
</text>
